Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS: no winemenubuilder. It turns every shortcut an installer
; makes into a Linux .desktop file -- and where the Desktop is not a Linux
; one, it writes that file into the Windows Desktop itself: Firefox's
; installer left "Firefox.desktop" beside the Firefox shortcut. Start and the
; desktop show the shortcuts; there is no Linux menu to feed. Disabled for
; every user (wine-sg reads HKLM's DllOverrides).

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Wine\DllOverrides]
"winemenubuilder.exe"=""
